{"parentUuid":"59dba334-4444-4de2-9e8e-0961b2bdd141","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyhk3g9SstNmCi8SKwhn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the review and the layout plan into `PLAN.md`. It isn't committed yet, so you can read it first. Light and dark mode is in phase L1.\n\n**Is it understandable?** Partly. The model underneath is sound, but the screens don't show it.\n- **Ten top-bar entries of equal weight.** Jobs, which you use daily, sits beside Engine and Verification, which you open rarely.\n- **Too many words for one idea.** Constraint, capability, permission, grant, rule, note, check, hook, reviewer, item, feedforward, feedback, rung, layer, harness, factory, dial and lights-on/dark.\n- **One change, five places.** A model is set on the step and in Settings. MCP servers are set in Settings but used in Permissions. The factory lines show in Permissions but are set somewhere else, and they are global, which breaks D58.\n\n**Is it useful?** Yes. The request → workflow → job → decision → landing loop works, governance is strong, and the records can span servers.\n\n**Is it easy to use?** Not yet:\n- There is no first-run path.\n- New request is a separate page, away from the jobs it adds to.\n- Pages explain themselves in long paragraphs (the Workspaces lede is about 120 words) instead of in the controls.\n\n**The proposed layout:**\n- **The bar:** `Jobs · Map · Workflows · Workspaces · Harness · Insights · Server`, plus a light/dark toggle. The server switcher stays as it is.\n- **Jobs is home.** It has the new-request form inline and one inbox of decisions: waiting jobs, held calls, and charter branches to merge.\n- **Job page.** It shows progress first, with one line for \"what this job waits for\". \"Change it from here\" lets a refused call offer \"Allow this at this step\", and a step offer \"Edit this step\" or \"Add a rule here\". That's how you make a specific change without knowing which page holds it.\n- **Map.** It's the visual map you asked about. Each server shows its workspaces, its workflows and their steps, and its harness, with lines from each item to the steps it applies at. Clicking a node opens its editor in a side panel.\n- **Harness.** One list with a kind filter. The app uses plain words: Guidance (feedforward), Check (feedback), Permission and Tool. MCP servers move there as tools.\n- **Insights** holds Audit Log, Costs, Evals and Verification. **Server** holds people, models and providers, notifications, history and engine health.\n\n**Hidden things I found, which have no name or no home yet:**\n- **Request with parts:** jobs already carry `parent`, `part` and `after_job`.\n- **Attempt:** each retry or send-back is a pass with its own turns and cost.\n- **Decision:** one inbox for everything a person must decide.\n- **Landing:** how a job ends, which should be a workspace policy.\n- **Model choice:** set on the server, the job and the step.\n- **Tool:** MCP servers, engine functions and commands.\n- **Kit:** an agent with its skills, hooks and MCP servers, which answers the plugins question.\n- **Lesson:** an escape found after landing becomes a check.\n- **Experiment:** \"try this rule on the last 10 requests\" before it goes live.\n- **Proposal:** a charter branch or a new workflow version waiting to be accepted.\n\n**Phases:** L1 words and theme, L2 the bar, L3 Jobs as home, L4 the job page, L5 the Map, L6 landing per workspace, L7 first run.\n\n**Questions for you:**\n1. Should Harness be one page with a kind filter? That would change D57's three tabs.\n2. Should the Map become where you set things up, with Workflows, Workspaces and Harness as its panels? My suggestion is to build the Map first and then decide.\n3. Can I rename the words in the app (Guidance, Check, Permission, Tool; \"who decides\" for the dial) and keep the precise terms only in DECISIONS.md?\n\nvoice-check reports one real finding on PLAN.md: it addresses the reader too little for an instruction page. The triad findings are data lists. I can also mock up the bar, the Jobs home and the Map as a page you can click through before any code changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":458435,"output_tokens":1452,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":62},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":458435,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"797ae270-439e-450c-a990-99fd8e3dc1bd","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgyhk3MYnerSishC1Xrn3","type":"assistant","uuid":"b789e6a1-e5b6-43d7-a551-44bb619eab89","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:57:39.836Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
