{"parentUuid":"a676142d-df5f-4023-8965-4633b1be0be5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyi2WarNKGJW5GRgBNCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan first: your three answers and plugins go into PLAN.md. Then I build the mockup."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":460320,"output_tokens":1919,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":392},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":289,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1919,"cache_read_input_tokens":460320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":289},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5ba91631-8235-44f4-9b8b-dec8bb4e6c7d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgyi2W5aWpkYgtHPwdkBY","type":"assistant","uuid":"71ec5d56-0af5-4e43-a31d-beec1c4443c4","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:01:14.943Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"71ec5d56-0af5-4e43-a31d-beec1c4443c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyi2WarNKGJW5GRgBNCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013PUM8oMLMvvd4Y1zFCUjtD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:60]; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep('''| **Tool** | Where calls go: the engine's functions, commands, MCP servers. | Harness |''','''| **Tool** | Where calls go: the engine's functions, commands, MCP servers. | Harness |\n| **Plugin** | An installed bundle of skills, agents, hooks and MCP servers. | Harness |''')\nrep('''- **Kit.** An agent, its skills, its hooks and its MCP servers, taken as\n  one. This answers the plugins question below.\n''','')\nrep('''## The layout\n''','''## Agent primitives: parity with Claude Code, kept small\n\nBastion offers the primitives a coding-agent harness offers, so a team's\nsetup moves over without a rewrite. One primitive is left out on purpose.\n\n| Claude Code | Bastion | Kind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` | Charter `AGENTS.md`, and rules a step is told | Guidance |\n| Skills | Skills: a charter's `.agents/skills`, or a plugin's | Guidance |\n| Subagents | Agents: a step that runs one, or a reviewer | Guidance, Check |\n| Hooks | Hooks before a call, and when a step ends | Check |\n| Permissions: allow, ask, deny | Permissions: allowed or ask; no grant refuses | Permission |\n| MCP servers | MCP servers, as tools a permission names | Tool |\n| Plugins and marketplaces | Plugins: installed per server, then applied | Plugin |\n| Output styles | Rules a step is told | Guidance |\n| Slash commands | Not a primitive: a shell step or a prompt step | none |\n\n**Plugins.** A plugin is a git repository with a manifest that lists its\nskills, agents, hooks and MCP servers, as a Claude Code plugin does. A\nperson installs it on a server, from a URL or a marketplace list, at a\npinned commit. Installing it adds nothing to a job: each part shows on the\nHarness page, off, and a person applies it to steps like any other item\n(D58). Updating a plugin is a new pinned commit, so a job always records\nwhich version ran. Caveman is the first plugin to try: its skills and its\nprompt hook map onto guidance and a hook.\n\n## The layout\n''')\nrep('''- MCP servers move here from Server, as tools.''','''- MCP servers move here from Server, as tools.\n- Plugins sit here too: Install, then each part listed under its plugin,\n  off until applied. Update and Remove are on the plugin.''')\nrep('''### L1. Words and theme''','''### L0. Mockup\n\n- A clickable mockup of the bar, Jobs, a job, the Map and the Harness, in\n  light and dark, before any code changes.\n\n### L1. Words and theme''')\nrep('''### L7. First run''','''### L7. Plugins\n\n- Install a plugin from a git URL at a pinned commit, on one server. Its\n  skills, agents, hooks and MCP servers show on Harness, off.\n- Each job records the plugin commits it ran with.\n\n### L8. First run''')\nrep('''- **Harness as one page.** D57 made three pages, then tabs. One page with a\n  kind filter is simpler to scan. Keep three, or merge?\n- **Map as the setup home.** If the map edits well, Workflows, Workspaces\n  and Harness could become its panels. Try the map first, then decide.\n- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a kit (an agent, its skills,\n  its hooks and its MCP servers) that a step takes as one?\n''','''- **Plugin hooks that need the host.** A Claude Code hook runs on the\n  person's machine; a Bastion hook runs in the job's VM. A plugin hook that\n  expects the host's files or tools may not work there.\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Open questions\" -A2 PLAN.md | head -3","description":"Plan: plugins, parity table, L0 mockup, answers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":460320,"output_tokens":1919,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":392},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":289,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1919,"cache_read_input_tokens":460320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":289},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013PUM8oMLMvvd4Y1zFCUjtD":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:60]; s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep('''| **Tool** | Where calls go: the engine's functions, commands, MCP servers. | Harness |''','''| **Tool** | Where calls go: the engine's functions, commands, MCP servers. | Harness |\n| **Plugin** | An installed bundle of skills, agents, hooks and MCP servers. | Harness |''')\nrep('''- **Kit.** An agent, its skills, its hooks and its MCP servers, taken as\n  one. This answers the plugins question below.\n''','')\nrep('''## The layout\n''','''## Agent primitives: parity with Claude Code, kept small\n\nBastion offers the primitives a coding-agent harness offers, so a team's\nsetup moves over without a rewrite. One primitive is left out on purpose.\n\n| Claude Code | Bastion | Kind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md` | Charter `AGENTS.md`, and rules a step is told | Guidance |\n| Skills | Skills: a charter's `.agents/skills`, or a plugin's | Guidance |\n| Subagents | Agents: a step that runs one, or a reviewer | Guidance, Check |\n| Hooks | Hooks before a call, and when a step ends | Check |\n| Permissions: allow, ask, deny | Permissions: allowed or ask; no grant refuses | Permission |\n| MCP servers | MCP servers, as tools a permission names | Tool |\n| Plugins and marketplaces | Plugins: installed per server, then applied | Plugin |\n| Output styles | Rules a step is told | Guidance |\n| Slash commands | Not a primitive: a shell step or a prompt step | none |\n\n**Plugins.** A plugin is a git repository with a manifest that lists its\nskills, agents, hooks and MCP servers, as a Claude Code plugin does. A\nperson installs it on a server, from a URL or a marketplace list, at a\npinned commit. Installing it adds nothing to a job: each part shows on the\nHarness page, off, and a person applies it to steps like any other item\n(D58). Updating a plugin is a new pinned commit, so a job always records\nwhich version ran. Caveman is the first plugin to try: its skills and its\nprompt hook map onto guidance and a hook.\n\n## The layout\n''')\nrep('''- MCP servers move here from Server, as tools.''','''- MCP servers move here from Server, as tools.\n- Plugins sit here too: Install, then each part listed under its plugin,\n  off until applied. Update and Remove are on the plugin.''')\nrep('''### L1. Words and theme''','''### L0. Mockup\n\n- A clickable mockup of the bar, Jobs, a job, the Map and the Harness, in\n  light and dark, before any code changes.\n\n### L1. Words and theme''')\nrep('''### L7. First run''','''### L7. Plugins\n\n- Install a plugin from a git URL at a pinned commit, on one server. Its\n  skills, agents, hooks and MCP servers show on Harness, off.\n- Each job records the plugin commits it ran with.\n\n### L8. First run''')\nrep('''- **Harness as one page.** D57 made three pages, then tabs. One page with a\n  kind filter is simpler to scan. Keep three, or merge?\n- **Map as the setup home.** If the map edits well, Workflows, Workspaces\n  and Harness could become its panels. Try the map first, then decide.\n- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a kit (an agent, its skills,\n  its hooks and its MCP servers) that a step takes as one?\n''','''- **Plugin hooks that need the host.** A Claude Code hook runs on the\n  person's machine; a Bastion hook runs in the job's VM. A plugin hook that\n  expects the host's files or tools may not work there.\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Open questions\" -A2 PLAN.md | head -3","description":"Plan: plugins, parity table, L0 mockup, answers"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5ba91631-8235-44f4-9b8b-dec8bb4e6c7d","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgyi2W5aWpkYgtHPwdkBY","type":"assistant","uuid":"2e74adec-4fb6-4d23-829b-c7aaf827b900","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:01:27.951Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
