{"parentUuid":"86a73410-d9b8-4906-8460-6dbc22373847","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c05ae742-b7ea-4081-ac5f-2b7df3580a90","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KoDe3QCMByX4QaVNUMiM76","type":"tool_result","content":"# Bastion's vision\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nBastion is an agent control plane. On each server, it manages a harness and\na factory: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent works under,\nand the workflows that run it. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a\njob through a workflow. The cost is plain: a job does only what its workflow\nsays, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone. Bastion runs on your\nmachine, on a remote server, or on both.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0c075efe-c6bd-4168-b655-e9d443e30704","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:11:55.155Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Bastion's vision\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nBastion is an agent control plane. On each server, it manages a harness and\na factory: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent works under,\nand the workflows that run it. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a\njob through a workflow. The cost is plain: a job does only what its workflow\nsays, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone. Bastion runs on your\nmachine, on a remote server, or on both.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"41be43f7-7630-4fb4-8329-2d1c1b9d81aa","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"86a73410-d9b8-4906-8460-6dbc22373847","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"0c075efe-c6bd-4168-b655-e9d443e30704","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01KoDe3QCMByX4QaVNUMiM76","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4945d3e7-9b56-46ab-98c6-7e16a361d010","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:12:11.164Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"4945d3e7-9b56-46ab-98c6-7e16a361d010","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyir8tx3RBpw2qJ8b41t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RMM1Ma1DSaR6b89pV67aRS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, (p, a[:60]); s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('VISION.md',[('''Bastion is an agent control plane. On each server, it manages a harness and\na factory: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent works under,\nand the workflows that run it. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a\njob through a workflow.''','''Bastion is an orchestration control plane for coding agents. Its\ndifference is the workflows: you define as many as your work needs, each a\nroute of steps with its own people, models and rules, and every request\npicks one. On each server, Bastion manages the harness and the factory\nthose routes run on: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent\nworks under. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a job along its\nworkflow.''')])\nedit('PLAN.md',[('''## The layout\n''','''## The look and feel: an expedition\n\n[The software expedition](https://blog.tacoda.dev/the-software-expedition-ca3631d61530)\ngives the app its picture. Every landmark in it is already a thing in\nBastion, so the app draws them without new words: a person never has to\nsay \"summit\" to use it.\n\n| On the map | In Bastion |\n|---|---|\n| The outpost | Where requests arrive: Jobs, an issue, a schedule |\n| The summit | The outcome a job must reach, picked before it leaves |\n| The guide | The harness: models, tools, the loop |\n| Base camp | The job's worktree and VM |\n| The charter | The workspace's charter (the same word) |\n| The checkpoint | A commit the checks passed |\n| The range of reality | Failing checks, a reviewer, a person sending work back |\n| The final peak | The job lands |\n| The track | The turns and the audit log |\n| Specimens | The change and its artifacts |\n| Field notes | What the job taught, one sentence signed by a person |\n| The marsh | A job stopped or failed, said out loud |\n| The atlas | Everything learned, where the next request starts |\n\nWhat this changes in the app:\n\n- **A job is a trail, not a list.** The job page draws the route: the\n  workflow's steps as landmarks, each pass back as a peak climbed again,\n  each commit the checks passed as a checkpoint. Where the job is now is a\n  marker on the trail.\n- **Workflows are routes.** Bastion's difference is many workflows, so the\n  Map draws them as routes across a server's ground, from the outpost to\n  the final peak, and a request picks its route at the outpost.\n- **Field notes are a new thing.** When a job lands or stops, a person can\n  sign one sentence: what reality said. A stopped job asks for one, so the\n  marsh is said out loud. Notes feed the atlas, the start of the next\n  request.\n- **A third theme, `bastion-chart`.** The old-world chart's parchment and\n  ink, for people who want the map to look like one. Ink #3b2a1a, paper\n  #efe4c8, red #9b2c1f.\n- **Tactile.** Landmarks are things to press: hover lifts them, a step on\n  the trail opens in place, and a route can be followed with the keys.\n\n## The layout\n'''),\n('''- **Lesson.** An escape found after a job landed should become a check, so\n  the same miss can't land twice. Verification and the harness meet here.''','''- **Lesson.** An escape found after a job landed should become a check, so\n  the same miss can't land twice. Verification and the harness meet here.\n- **Field note.** What a job taught, signed by a person when it lands or\n  stops. Together the notes are the atlas.\n- **Outcome.** A job already keeps `criteria`: the summit picked before it\n  leaves. The job page should show it first.'''),\n('''### L2. The bar''','''### L1b. The chart theme\n\n- `bastion-chart`, beside the first two.\n\n### L2. The bar'''),\n])\nEOF\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py VISION.md 2>&1 | sed -n 1,4p; git add VISION.md PLAN.md && git commit -q -m \"Vision: an orchestration control plane; plan: the expedition look\n\nBastion's difference is many workflows, each a route a request picks.\nThe software expedition gives the app its picture: a job drawn as a\ntrail, workflows as routes on the Map, field notes signed by a person,\nand a bastion-chart theme.\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Vision lede; expedition section in plan; commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1244,"cache_read_input_tokens":540673,"output_tokens":1627,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1244,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1627,"cache_read_input_tokens":540673,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1244},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RMM1Ma1DSaR6b89pV67aRS":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef edit(p, pairs):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, (p, a[:60]); s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n    open(p,'w').write(s)\nedit('VISION.md',[('''Bastion is an agent control plane. On each server, it manages a harness and\na factory: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent works under,\nand the workflows that run it. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a\njob through a workflow.''','''Bastion is an orchestration control plane for coding agents. Its\ndifference is the workflows: you define as many as your work needs, each a\nroute of steps with its own people, models and rules, and every request\npicks one. On each server, Bastion manages the harness and the factory\nthose routes run on: the rules, agents, skills, hooks and grants an agent\nworks under. You send a request, and Bastion runs it as a job along its\nworkflow.''')])\nedit('PLAN.md',[('''## The layout\n''','''## The look and feel: an expedition\n\n[The software expedition](https://blog.tacoda.dev/the-software-expedition-ca3631d61530)\ngives the app its picture. Every landmark in it is already a thing in\nBastion, so the app draws them without new words: a person never has to\nsay \"summit\" to use it.\n\n| On the map | In Bastion |\n|---|---|\n| The outpost | Where requests arrive: Jobs, an issue, a schedule |\n| The summit | The outcome a job must reach, picked before it leaves |\n| The guide | The harness: models, tools, the loop |\n| Base camp | The job's worktree and VM |\n| The charter | The workspace's charter (the same word) |\n| The checkpoint | A commit the checks passed |\n| The range of reality | Failing checks, a reviewer, a person sending work back |\n| The final peak | The job lands |\n| The track | The turns and the audit log |\n| Specimens | The change and its artifacts |\n| Field notes | What the job taught, one sentence signed by a person |\n| The marsh | A job stopped or failed, said out loud |\n| The atlas | Everything learned, where the next request starts |\n\nWhat this changes in the app:\n\n- **A job is a trail, not a list.** The job page draws the route: the\n  workflow's steps as landmarks, each pass back as a peak climbed again,\n  each commit the checks passed as a checkpoint. Where the job is now is a\n  marker on the trail.\n- **Workflows are routes.** Bastion's difference is many workflows, so the\n  Map draws them as routes across a server's ground, from the outpost to\n  the final peak, and a request picks its route at the outpost.\n- **Field notes are a new thing.** When a job lands or stops, a person can\n  sign one sentence: what reality said. A stopped job asks for one, so the\n  marsh is said out loud. Notes feed the atlas, the start of the next\n  request.\n- **A third theme, `bastion-chart`.** The old-world chart's parchment and\n  ink, for people who want the map to look like one. Ink #3b2a1a, paper\n  #efe4c8, red #9b2c1f.\n- **Tactile.** Landmarks are things to press: hover lifts them, a step on\n  the trail opens in place, and a route can be followed with the keys.\n\n## The layout\n'''),\n('''- **Lesson.** An escape found after a job landed should become a check, so\n  the same miss can't land twice. Verification and the harness meet here.''','''- **Lesson.** An escape found after a job landed should become a check, so\n  the same miss can't land twice. Verification and the harness meet here.\n- **Field note.** What a job taught, signed by a person when it lands or\n  stops. Together the notes are the atlas.\n- **Outcome.** A job already keeps `criteria`: the summit picked before it\n  leaves. The job page should show it first.'''),\n('''### L2. The bar''','''### L1b. The chart theme\n\n- `bastion-chart`, beside the first two.\n\n### L2. The bar'''),\n])\nEOF\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py VISION.md 2>&1 | sed -n 1,4p; git add VISION.md PLAN.md && git commit -q -m \"Vision: an orchestration control plane; plan: the expedition look\n\nBastion's difference is many workflows, each a route a request picks.\nThe software expedition gives the app its picture: a job drawn as a\ntrail, workflows as routes on the Map, field notes signed by a person,\nand a bastion-chart theme.\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Vision lede; expedition section in plan; commit"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01RMM1Ma1DSaR6b89pV67aRS":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f85bf8e9-1603-4d5a-a265-ce1df44f05b5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgyir8YsXiUdUTYnfeKKr","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e4d4882-cb0e-467a-85c2-6f3483db0f2a","timestamp":"2026-11-12T21:12:11.163Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
